1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:01,580
Business reporters have a

2
00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:03,560
better word than "good."

3
00:00:03,560 --> 00:00:04,700
Buoyant.

4
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:05,820
BOY-uhnt.

5
00:00:05,820 --> 00:00:08,240
Stress on the first syllable.

6
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:10,820
Buoyant means it floats.

7
00:00:10,820 --> 00:00:11,750
In business,

8
00:00:11,750 --> 00:00:14,440
it means rising and optimistic.

9
00:00:14,440 --> 00:00:15,290
For example,

10
00:00:15,290 --> 00:00:19,060
"The labour market remains buoyant despite layoffs."

11
00:00:19,060 --> 00:00:19,710
At work,

12
00:00:19,710 --> 00:00:21,200
swap "good" for "buoyant":

13
00:00:21,200 --> 00:00:24,420
"Sales are buoyant this quarter."

14
00:00:24,420 --> 00:00:26,340
Try this word in your next email,

15
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:27,860
follow The Fluent Edge

16
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:30,220
for more workplace vocabulary.
